# GCALENDAR.md — Google Calendar Reference

{{USER_NAME}}'s primary personal calendar is a dedicated personal calendar (the `personal` entry in `connectors.yaml`), not the default Gmail primary calendar. **Always pass the calendar ID explicitly** — the no-ID form silently hits `primary`, which is the wrong calendar for personal events.

---

## The Rule: MCP is primary (read **and** write), gog-firewall is the fallback

| Goal | Use | Why |
|------|-----|-----|
| **Everything** — list, get, search, create, update, delete, respond, free/busy | **MCP Calendar tools** (`mcp__claude_ai_Google_Calendar__*`) | Native, structured JSON, available in every {{PERSONA_NAME}} run (incl. headless crons), full read **and** write scopes. This is the default for all calendar work. |
| **Fallback** — *only* when an MCP call returns an **auth error** (connector token lapsed) | **`gog-firewall calendar` CLI** | Uses gog's own long-lived OAuth, which survives independently of the claude.ai connector. Keeps cron jobs alive when the MCP token expires. |

Unlike Gmail (where MCP can't write, so writes stay on the CLI), **MCP Calendar handles writes fine** — create/update/delete/respond all work. So calendar is MCP-first across the board.

**When you hit the fallback:** if a calendar MCP call fails with an authentication/authorization error, (1) fall back to the equivalent `gog-firewall calendar` command for this run, and (2) note that {{USER_NAME}} should run `claude mcp login "claude.ai Google Calendar"` in an interactive session to restore the connector. Don't silently drop the calendar — degrade to gog.

