## Fallback: `gog-firewall calendar` (only on MCP auth error)

The full gog calendar surface still works via gog's own OAuth. Use it **only** when an MCP call returns an auth/authorization error, then tell {{USER_NAME}} to re-login the connector. Tool path: `{{MINERU_HOME}}/bin/gog-firewall`.

```bash
# List a window (accepts --from/--to RFC3339-or-date, or --days N, or --today/--tomorrow/--week)
{{MINERU_HOME}}/bin/gog-firewall calendar events \
  {{PERSONAL_CALENDAR_ID}} --from "2026-06-29" --to "2026-07-06" --json

# Get one event (the "get" verb is implicit — do NOT write "event get")
{{MINERU_HOME}}/bin/gog-firewall calendar event \
  {{PERSONAL_CALENDAR_ID}} <eventId>

# Create / update / delete (always pass --location on create; --no-input for scripted writes)
{{MINERU_HOME}}/bin/gog-firewall calendar create {{PERSONAL_CALENDAR_ID}} \
  --summary "…" --from "2026-07-02T18:30:00-07:00" --to "2026-07-02T20:30:00-07:00" \
  --location "…" --no-input
{{MINERU_HOME}}/bin/gog-firewall calendar update <CAL> <eventId> --location "…" --no-input
{{MINERU_HOME}}/bin/gog-firewall calendar delete <CAL> <eventId> --no-input
```

gog fallback gotchas (when you're in this path): the wrapper injects `--max 500`; a list read lives under `.events[]` (a single read under `.event`) — **not** `.items[]`; `update` is partial; `--attendees` replaces while `--add-attendee` adds; `event` get is implicit (no `get` verb). Restore MCP afterward with `claude mcp login "claude.ai Google Calendar"`.

---

## Anti-Patterns (do not do)

```
# WRONG — omits calendarId, hits the primary Gmail calendar instead of the personal calendar
mcp__claude_ai_Google_Calendar__list_events  startTime: "…"  endTime: "…"

# WRONG — relative words aren't valid; compute ISO datetimes from `date` first
mcp__claude_ai_Google_Calendar__list_events  startTime: "today"  endTime: "tomorrow"

# WRONG — reaching for gog first. MCP is primary; gog is only the auth-error fallback.
gog-firewall calendar events <CAL> --days 7

# WRONG — no location on a personal event
mcp__claude_ai_Google_Calendar__create_event  summary: "Lunch"  startTime: "…"  endTime: "…"
```
